From 5f36a17bc43b8e43e666fb508568354c15a06645 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xz-dev <xiangzhedev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 16:53:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: blank wide graphemes straddling popup edges

Overlay drawing (settings, menus, toasts, copy feedback, banners, popup
panes) can overwrite the trailing cell of a wide grapheme from the
underlying content while the leading cell stays just outside the
overlay. The blit encoder suppresses the cell following any wide
grapheme (to_skip), so the stale grapheme kept rendering across the
overlay edge and swallowed the popup border on that row.

Blank the leading half of any wide grapheme sitting immediately left of
an overlay rect, at each painter that covers content. The check is
geometric, so it cannot touch legitimate text and does not depend on
the trailing-cell symbol, which is not a stable contract across server
versions (a 0.9.0 server sends " " there once a hyperlink on screen
forces the full-frame fallback).

refs #1555
